# {{PROJECT}} Knowledge — README & Charter

> **TL;DR:** One shared knowledge base for every agent: check its verification status, retrieve relevant claims, and keep durable facts with their evidence.

**KB status:** {{STATUS_LINE}}

Single source of truth for ALL agents (claude, codex, cursor, factory, gstack, hermes, whatever comes next) working on {{PROJECT}}. Files beat agent-native memory: markdown + git is the only substrate every agent reads natively, it diffs, reviews, and survives tool churn.

## The status line (read this first)

- `SCAFFOLDED` — structure only, **do not cite as truth**. A `knowledge/_bootstrap-brief.md` should exist; completing it is the highest-priority task for the first agent session.
- `VERIFIED @ <commit>` — distilled with per-claim evidence. You may cite it; recheck runtime claims against the environment before operational work.

The status line lives here and in [INDEX.md](INDEX.md); both must agree. Flip it to VERIFIED only after a distillation pass, naming a real commit — `scripts/knowledge-gate.py` enforces this at commit time.

## Labels

Every factual claim in `docs/` and `memory/` carries a label: ✅ VERIFIED (evidence cited: file, command output, commit) · ❓ UNVERIFIED (stated but not checked). Dated records may carry ⚠ STALE for claims their sources have outlived — stale material belongs in `archive/`, never cited as current.

## Layout

| Dir | Contents |
|---|---|
| `rules/` | hard constraints — behavior, quality gates, boundaries |
| `practices/` | how we build — commands, conventions |
| `docs/` | verified architecture, specs (current truth) |
| `memory/` | durable operational facts — environments, incidents |
| `learning/` | append-only dated lessons log + distilled pitfalls |
| `plans/` | active work and handoffs — see the [status board](plans/README.md) |
| `agents/<name>/` | per-agent wiring only (tool-specific syntax, nothing else) |
| `archive/` | superseded material — history, never cite as current |

Entry point for every session: [INDEX.md](INDEX.md). Search before reading: `scripts/ksearch.py "<query>"`.

## Charter (short)

1. Default is DON'T write — record only what a future session would otherwise re-derive painfully or dangerously.
2. Knowledge commits ride with the code that taught them.
3. Stale code/docs found during work get removed in the same commit.
4. Agent-native memory holds routing pointers only, never project knowledge.
5. Don't duplicate — `ksearch` first, patch the existing file.

Full policies: [rules/](rules/). The design behind this layout: [docs/agent-memory-architecture.md](docs/agent-memory-architecture.md).
